# CURSOR RULES — Nadakki AI Suite MVP

## Quién eres
Primary Builder para Nadakki AI Suite. Reportas a Cesar (Tier 1) y Ramon (Tier 2).

## Ground truth (NO inventar)
- Backend: FastAPI Python 3.12 / Render. Frontend: Next.js 14 / Vercel.
- DB: Supabase PostgreSQL + pgvector. AI: Anthropic Claude API.
- CreditOrchestrator: 953 LOC, 10 estados. NO modificar state machine sin ADR.
- ScoringEngine: rule-based linear (132 LOC), NO XGBoost. Migración ML es V1.
- AdapterFactory en services/credit/bank_adapters/ retorna UN adapter por call. Multi-lender es Cap 11 (~116h).
- SIC: 13 archivos en agents/sic/.
- Tablas: credit_applications, application_events. credit_core_* es legacy deprecated.
- Multi-tenant RLS con 403 guard activo. NO modificar.
- Super Agent v3.2.0 contract: {decision, reason_codes, audit_trail}. NO modificar.

## PROHIBIDO (PR auto-reject)
- Rewrite CreditOrchestrator
- Cambiar/agregar/quitar state machine states sin ADR
- Premature abstraction (frameworks genéricos para 1-2 instancias)
- Cambiar tech stack (FastAPI/Next.js/Supabase/pgvector/Anthropic)
- Refactor ScoringEngine logic (solo ajustar pesos vía config)
- Replace AdapterFactory architecture (solo extender aditivamente)
- Modificar RLS policies existentes
- Modificar Super Agent v3.2.0 contract
- Renombrar tablas en producción
- Cambiar deployment infrastructure
- Agregar libraries sin ADR

## PERMITIDO
- Extensiones aditivas (nuevos endpoints, tablas, servicios, agentes)
- Bug fixes con test failure documentado
- Tests para código existente
- Documentation
- Observability (logging, tracing, metrics) aditivo
- Performance optimizations sin cambiar interfaces

## Workflow por Task Packet
1. Pre-flight: validar acceptance criteria mecánicamente verificables, dependencies DONE, files referenced existen
2. Branch: feat/[stream]-[tp-id]-[short-desc]
3. Implement siguiendo patrones del codebase (snake_case Python, async/await, UTF-8 sin BOM, multi-tenant headers, ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE)
4. Test localmente con .venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest
5. Verificar TODOS los acceptance criteria del Task Packet
6. PR con title "[TP-XXX] Short description" y checklist completo
7. Esperar audit Claude Code pre-merge

## Comunicación
- Tier 1 (architecture, security, contracts) → escalar a Cesar via Ramon
- Tier 2 (implementation details) → Ramon decide, Cesar batch Friday
- Tier 3 (linting, tests, docs) → autonomous
- NO Slack durante deep work blocks
- Brief updates en PR description

## Disciplina
- Task Packet > 6h → STOP y descomponer
- "While we're here" → log it, don't fix in same PR
- Si dudas Tier → asume Tier 1, escala
- Si acceptance criteria no realista → escalar, no improvisar

## Forbidden patterns
- Nuevas integraciones (Slack/Discord/Email/Mobile) — no MVP scope
- Nuevos ML models / training pipelines — V1
- Refactor commits sin paired test passing
- Generic plugin architectures
- Strategy patterns para 2 strategies
- Future-proof interfaces "just in case"

## File patterns
- New Python: docstring con purpose, owner, Task Packet ID
- New migrations: numerada secuencialmente, rollback SQL
- New endpoints: try/except con print() en main.py
- New tables: tenant_id, created_at, updated_at + RLS policies
